/* =====================================================================
   bea-two-bookshelves-core.js — the model for ACTIVITY #118 of the
   one-by-one rebuild: "Bea's Two Bookshelves" → THE SHAKER SHELF AND
   THE RIBBON SHELF (RL.1.5; all 11 locales).
   Design: docs/activities-rebuild/designs/118-bea-two-bookshelves.md
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bea's two shelves test a book the way the books themselves are made.
   The ribbon shelf threads a ribbon through a book's pages from the
   beginning to the end: only a story has a beginning and an end to tie.
   The shaker shelf shakes a book's pages into a new order: an all-about
   fact book still makes sense, because every page stands on its own; a
   story comes out ending first and no longer makes sense.
   · Levels: Bea asks (the kept rounds) · Same topic (two books on one
     topic, one of each kind — topic can never decide) · Fill both
     shelves (four books, two of each kind, no ask).
   · Fifteen books per locale, each with three inside pages. DATA is
     written by a build script that checks every story for a beginning
     and an ending and every fact page for a heading and no sequence word.
   Pure and DOM-free; UMD (window.BeaShelvesCore / require()).
   ===================================================================== */
